+ * IOBlockStorageDevice dispatch table was measured in the donor kernelcache
+ * and in the prelinked candidate (see docs/BRING-UP-STATE.md, section 87).
+ * The iOS class has exactly 22 virtual methods of its own, in the order below,
+ * and no OSMetaClass reserved padding slots:
+ *
+ *   doEjectMedia, doFormatMedia, doGetFormatCapacities, doLockUnlockMedia,
+ *   getVendorString, getProductString, getRevisionString,
+ *   getAdditionalDeviceInfoString, reportBlockSize, reportEjectability,
+ *   reportMaxValidBlock, reportMediaState, reportRemovability,
+ *   reportWriteProtection, getWriteCacheState, setWriteCacheState,
+ *   doAsyncReadWrite, requestIdle, doUnmap, doSetPriority, doSynchronize,
+ *   doGetProvisionStatus
