+ * The macOS header also declares doSynchronizeCache, reportLockability,
+ * reportPollRequirements and doDiscard, which the iOS binary does not have.
+ * They are removed here so a subclass vtable lines up with the runtime class.
+ * doLockUnlockMedia is kept (and unguarded) because the iOS binary does have
+ * that slot. The reserved-slot declarations are dropped for the same reason.
+ *
+ * Everything else is Apple's text, unchanged.
+ */
